                        calendar="#gregorian">s. xii/xiii</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#e" cert="low" source="4042"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_398"
                        >Newstead, Lincolnshire. Augustinian priory of St Mary the
                        Virgin</orgName><p>'Explicit vtum volumen moral' Gregorii a magistro
                        Gaufredo de Lard' da(tum) Sancte Marie de Novo Loco (fol. 12v, s. xii/xiii).
                        'Liber Sancte Marie de Nouo Loco' (fol. 1v, in red).</p><p>Bodleian, Laud
                        Misc. 428 and Laud Misc. 285 may have belonged to Newstead, Lincs., or more
                        probably, Newstead, Notts., since it came to Laud from William le Neve, like
                        Laud Lat. 34. Compare the initial in Laud misc 285, another Le Neve book and
                        ? also flyleaves.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="#e" cert="low" source="6380"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_396"
                        >Newstead, Nottinghamshire. Augustinian priory of St Mary the
                        Virgin</orgName><p>See above.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_399">Newstead, Lincolnshire.
                        Gilbertine priory of Holy Trinity</orgName><p>This attribution was
                        erroneously(?) included in MLGB3 with the following note: see under
                        Newstead, Nottinghamshire. However, MS Laud Misc. 428 was not attributed to
                        the Gilbertine priory of Holy Trinity in Newstead, Lincolnshire in either
                        MLGB2 or the Supplement. It appears that two houses in Newstead,
                        Lincolnshire may have been conflated: the Gilbertine priory of Holy Trinity
                        and the Augustinian priory of St Mary the Virgin.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><persName>William le
                     Neve</persName>.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><persName>Laud</persName> 1639.</provenance>
               </history>
